From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:49:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: native settings pages - System, LAN, WAN, VPN, Parental,
 logs and tools

Reaper's own pages for System (and SNMP, Tweaks), the System Log group (log,
wireless log, leases, routes, port forwards, IPv6, analysis, netstat, wake on
LAN), LAN (DHCP, switch), WAN (Internet, NAT, DDNS, IPv6 setup, IPTV, DNS,
Smart Connect), VPN (status, VPN Director, server, client, Tor) and Parental
Controls time scheduling. Each was compared field by field with the stock page
it replaces (posted names and values, the stock validations); secrets are never
placed in the page source. Deep links take ?tab=.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
