+     Replaces DNSDirector.asp (parity file build-scripts/tests/ui_parity/DNSDirector.json) and takes over the DNS
+     rows of two other stock pages: the DNS / WINS server rows of Advanced_DHCP_Content.asp, and the WAN DNS block +
+     DNS-over-TLS client of sysdep/FUNCTION/MULTISERVICE_WAN/Advanced_WAN_Content.asp (the Internet page only links here).
+     Three tabs by direction: Router upstream (what the router asks), Handed to clients (what DHCP gives devices),
+     DNS Director (forced redirection). The DoT SERVER and the encrypted-DNS blocking live on Reaper_EncryptedDNS.asp,
+     linked, not repeated. Only the changed settings are posted; nothing is written on load.
+     Restarts (rc citations at applyAll): WAN DNS servers restart_wan_dns <unit> (what the stock WAN page's DNS popup ran,
+     without the WAN restart its Apply did); resolver options and client DNS restart_dnsmasq; the DoT client
+     restart_stubby (+ restart_wan_dns 0;restart_dnsmasq when it is switched on or off); DNS Director restart_dnsfilter.
+     Deliberate differences from stock:
+     - DNS Director: the three IPv4 custom servers are validated (stock never checked them, B-DNSD-1), a MAC can only
+       have one rule (B-DNSD-2), and the Guest Network Pro profile column is written into a FRESH read of sdn_rl at
+       Apply, only for the profiles edited (stock re-posted the whole sdn_rl from page-load state, B-DNSD-3).
+     - DHCP: dhcp_dns2_x is validated (stock did not, B-DHCP-1); the DNS rows restart dnsmasq, not the whole network.
