+<!-- Reaper_IPTV.asp - LAN > IPTV (Reaper-native UI, LAN/WAN wave, 2026-10-23).
+     Replaces Advanced_IPTV_Content.asp (parity file build-scripts/tests/ui_parity/Advanced_IPTV_Content.json).
+     The ISP profile list, STB port list and port names come from the same httpd calls as stock (get_iptvSettings,
+     get_stbPortMappings); every stock check is kept (VLAN ID 2-4094, priority 0-7, the service
+     connection checks, the dual-WAN / bonding / SDN port conflicts) and the IPTV / VoIP service connections
+     (wan10_* / wan11_*) are edited in place instead of a popup.
+     Deliberate differences:
+     - nothing is written on load: stock called get_MS_WAN_list_Pri, which sets wan_unit=0 (httpd/web.c:52121); this page
+       reads wan101-107_enable directly.
+     - the Multi-Service WAN and 802.1Q conflict fixes are sent only after the final reboot confirm (stock sent them at
+       once with applyapp.cgi, even when the reboot was then cancelled), and the conflict questions are asked only when
+       the IPTV assignment itself changes (stock asked on every save while IPTV was on).
+     - the service connections' manual DNS servers are validated (stock: if(!x == "1") never ran, inventory B-IPTV-1),
+       and their passwords are never written into the page (stock embedded wan10/11_pppoe_passwd): a typed password
+       replaces the saved one, blank keeps it.
+     - choosing None after a profile starts with no STB port (stock kept the profile's port bridged, so None left IPTV on).
