+<!-- Reaper_Internet.asp - WAN > Internet Connection (Reaper-native UI, LAN/WAN wave, 2026-10-23).
+     Replaces the page that ships on every MULTISERVICE_WAN model, www/sysdep/FUNCTION/MULTISERVICE_WAN/Advanced_WAN_Content.asp
+     (copied over www/Advanced_WAN_Content.asp by www/Makefile), and Advanced_Modem_Content.asp as the USB unit's view.
+     Parity files: build-scripts/tests/ui_parity/Advanced_WAN_Content.json and Advanced_Modem_Content.json.
+     Same connection types (DHCP, static, PPPoE, PPTP, L2TP; v6plus / OCN / DS-Lite / IPv6 Option where the box reports
+     s46; Bridge for Multi-Service WAN profiles), the same row visibility and every stock check, plus the checks the
+     inventory flagged (VLAN ID 2-4094 and 802.1P 0-7 when 802.1Q is on, a 64-character VPN server field to match its
+     nvram size, MAC/host name/option-60/61 text checks, PPP echo numbers).
+     Deliberate differences:
+     - nothing is written on load: stock ran wan_get_parameter() (copies wan<N>_* into wan_* in nvram) and switching the
+       WAN unit posted change_wan_unit; this page reads wan0_* / wan1_* directly and switches units in the browser.
+     - only the changed settings are posted, with wan_unit so httpd maps wan_* to wan<N>_* (httpd/web.c validate_apply).
+     - a restart of the WAN is confirmed first, saying the internet drops and for how long; a reboot likewise.
+     - the WAN-aggregation save no longer throws (stock validForm wrote wans_dualwan / wans_mode inputs the form did not
+       have): this form has them, so turning aggregation on with dual WAN active really turns dual WAN off.
+     - the 802.1Q / IPTV conflict question is asked only when 802.1Q is turned on (stock asked on every save with IPTV on).
+     - Multi-Service WAN profiles are edited in the same editor and saved by Apply (stock saved them from a popup with
+       applyapp.cgi at once); deleting a profile posts only wan<1xx>_enable=0 (stock re-posted the whole main form).
+     - WAN DNS servers and the DNS-over-TLS client live on the DNS page (Reaper_DNS.asp); this page links there. A
+       switch to Static is refused until that WAN has DNS servers set by hand (stock forced the same through its popup).
+     - PPPoE / modem / service passwords are never written into the page: the field is blank and a typed value replaces
+       the saved one. The "show password" box shows only what was typed.
+     - UPnP-only changes run restart_firewall;restart_upnp and TTL-only changes restart_firewall instead of a WAN restart.
+     - IPTV cleared by a conflict answer reboots the router (the switch VLANs need it, as the IPTV page does).
