+<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+     Copyright (C) 2026 the Reaper project maintainer
+     Part of the Reaper hardened Asuswrt-Merlin build. See LICENSE / LICENSE.reaper. -->
+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+<meta charset="utf-8">
+<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
+<meta name="reaper-native" content="1">
+<title>REAPER &mdash; <#menu5_7_2#></title>
+<!-- Reaper_Log.asp - System Log > General Log (Reaper-native UI, System Log wave, 2026-10-23).
+     Replaces Main_LogStatus_Content.asp AND Main_Security_Change_Notification.asp (owner: the "Security Update
+     Notification" tab is really the login log - fold it in here). Two views:
+       System log - httpd ej_dump("syslog.log") through /appGet.cgi (the closed HND filter applies server side,
+                    /ajax/logFilter.json client side, as stock); Clear = apply.cgi action_mode " Clear " (httpd
+                    unlinks /jffs/syslog.log[-1] and writes a [LOG]:clear line to the login log); Save = syslog.txt
+                    (the unfiltered file, as stock).
+       Login log  - ej_dump("security_recored.log"): web logins, failures, captcha errors, log clears (closed
+                    libasuslog writer; read-only, as stock).
+     The appGet reply is not JSON ("nvram_dump-<file>": + raw text + "\n}\n"), so the text is cut at the first '":'
+     and the last "\n}" rather than at fixed offsets. Polling runs only while auto refresh is on and the page is
+     visible, and never redraws while the reader has scrolled up. Settings: the stock four (log_ipaddr, log_port,
+     message_loglevel, log_level), changed ones only, restart_logger. -->
+<link rel="stylesheet" href="/reaper/rp.css">
+<style>
+/* page-specific rules only; the Reaper look comes from /reaper/rp.css */
+.wins{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap}
+.logbar{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:0 0 12px}
+.logbar .spacer{flex:1}
+.logbar input[type=text]{background:#000;border:1px solid var(--line-soft);border-radius:8px;color:var(--bone);font-family:var(--body);font-size:13px;padding:8px 10px;outline:none;width:240px;max-width:100%}
+.logbar input[type=text]:focus{border-color:var(--line)}
+.logview{background:#000;border:1px solid var(--line-soft);border-radius:10px;color:var(--bone-dim);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;
+  padding:10px 12px;margin:0;height:60vh;min-height:280px;overflow:auto;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-all}
+.logmeta{font-size:12px;color:var(--steel);margin-top:8px;min-height:16px}
+.frow input.mid{width:260px}  .frow select{min-width:160px}
+.frow.bad input,.frow.bad select{border-color:var(--crimson)!important;box-shadow:0 0 0 2px rgba(225,6,0,.25)}
+.msg{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--amber);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;max-width:100%;min-width:0;display:none}
+.btns{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin-top:12px}
+.pagehead .mono{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--steel)}
+</style>
+</head>
+<body>
+<script src="/reaper_util.js"></script>
+<script src="/reaper/rp.js"></script>
+
+<div class="syswrap">
+<div class="pagehead">
+  <div>
+    <div class="eyebrow"><#System_Log#></div>
+    <h1><#menu5_7_2#></h1>
+  </div>
+  <span class="pill"><span class="dot"></span><span class="mono" id="systime"></span></span>
+  <span class="pill"><span class="mono"><#General_x_SystemUpTime_itemname#>: <span id="uptime"></span></span></span>
+  <div class="spacer"></div>
+</div>
+<div class="hint" style="margin:-4px 0 14px"><#GeneralLog_title#></div>
+
+<div class="rframe">
+<div class="panel" id="p_log">
+  <div class="logbar">
+    <div class="wins" id="wins">
+      <button type="button" class="win on" data-v="sys"><#RLOG_01#></button>
+      <button type="button" class="win" data-v="login"><#RLOG_02#></button>
+    </div>
+    <div class="spacer"></div>
+    <input type="text" id="find" placeholder="<#CTL_search#>" autocomplete="off">
+    <label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" id="c_auto" checked><#RLOG_03#></label>
+  </div>
+  <div class="secerr"><#RADM_78#></div>
+  <pre class="logview" id="logview"></pre>
+  <div class="logmeta" id="logmeta"></div>
+  <div class="btns">
+    <button type="button" class="btn" id="b_refresh"><#CTL_refresh#></button>
+    <button type="button" class="btn" id="b_save"><#CTL_onlysave#></button>
+    <button type="button" class="btn" id="b_clear"><#CTL_clear#></button>
+    <span class="msg" id="logmsg"></span>
+  </div>
+</div>
+
+<div class="panel" id="p_set">
+  <h2><#RLOG_04#></h2>
+  <div class="secerr"><#RADM_78#></div>
+  <div class="frow"><div class="fl"><#LANHostConfig_x_ServerLogEnable_itemname#></div><div class="fc"><input type="text" class="mid mono" id="i_log_ipaddr" maxlength="128" autocomplete="off"></div><div class="fh"><#RLOG_05#></div></div>
+  <div class="frow"><div class="fl"><#LANHostConfig_x_ServerLogPort_itemname#></div><div class="fc"><input type="text" class="short mono" id="i_log_port" maxlength="5"></div></div>
+  <div class="frow"><div class="fl"><#RLOG_06#></div><div class="fc"><select id="s_message_loglevel"></select></div><div class="fh"><#RLOG_07#></div></div>
+  <div class="frow"><div class="fl"><#RLOG_08#></div><div class="fc"><select id="s_log_level"></select></div><div class="fh"><#RLOG_09#></div></div>
+  <div class="btns">
+    <button type="button" class="btn primary" id="applybtn"><#CTL_apply#></button>
+    <button type="button" class="btn ghost" id="discardbtn" disabled><#Discard#></button>
+    <span class="msg" id="setmsg"></span>
+  </div>
+</div>
+</div>
+</div>
+
+<div class="applying" id="applying"><div class="abox"><h2 id="ap_t"><#Reaper_c_applying#></h2><p id="ap_p"><#RADM_61#></p></div></div>
+<iframe name="hidden_frame" id="hidden_frame" style="display:none" width="0" height="0"></iframe>
+<form method="post" name="form" action="/start_apply.htm" target="hidden_frame">
+  <input type="hidden" name="current_page" value="Reaper_Log.asp">
+  <input type="hidden" name="next_page" value="Reaper_Log.asp">
+  <input type="hidden" name="action_mode" value="apply">
+  <input type="hidden" name="action_script" value="restart_logger">
+  <input type="hidden" name="action_wait" value="5">
+  <input type="hidden" name="log_ipaddr" value="" disabled>
+  <input type="hidden" name="log_port" value="" disabled>
+  <input type="hidden" name="message_loglevel" value="" disabled>
+  <input type="hidden" name="log_level" value="" disabled>
+</form>
+<form method="post" name="clearform" action="/apply.cgi" target="hidden_frame">
+  <input type="hidden" name="current_page" value="Reaper_Log.asp">
+  <input type="hidden" name="action_mode" value=" Clear ">
+</form>
+
+<script>
+(function(){
+'use strict';
+/* everything stays inside this closure: a page-level name can shadow reaper_util.js's window.esc and friends */
+var q = rp.q, hx = rp.esc;
+var U = rp.dec, on = rp.on;   /* the kit's copies (rp.js) */
+
+var NV = {
+  log_ipaddr: U('<% nvram_char_to_ascii("","log_ipaddr"); %>'), log_port: '<% nvram_get("log_port"); %>',
+  message_loglevel: '<% nvram_get("message_loglevel"); %>', log_level: '<% nvram_get("log_level"); %>'
+};
+/* empty nvram = the default (shared/defaults.c) */
+(function(){ var D = {log_port: '514', message_loglevel: '5', log_level: '7'}, k; for (k in D) if (NV[k] === '') NV[k] = D[k]; })();
+var UPSTR = '<% uptime(); %>';
+var LEVELS = ['emergency', 'alert', 'critical', 'error', 'warning', 'notice', 'info', 'debug', 'all'];
+var HOOK = {sys: 'nvram_dump("syslog.log","")', login: 'nvram_dump("security_recored.log","")'};
+var view = 'sys', FILTER = ["already exist in UDB, can't add it", "not mesh client, can't update it's ip", "not exist in UDB, can't update it", 'send_redir_page'];
+var timer = null, busy = false, lastText = {sys: null, login: null};
+
+function msg(id, t){ var m = q(id); m.textContent = t || ''; m.classList.toggle('show', !!t); if (t) m.setAttribute('title', t); }
+
+/* ---------- clock + uptime (router time: tick the router's own wall clock, not the browser's zone) ---------- */
+function clock(){
+  var p = rp.pad2;
+  rp.clock(UPSTR, function(d, s){
+    if (d) q('systime').textContent = d.getUTCFullYear() + '-' + p(d.getUTCMonth() + 1) + '-' + p(d.getUTCDate()) + ' ' + p(d.getUTCHours()) + ':' + p(d.getUTCMinutes()) + ':' + p(d.getUTCSeconds());
+    if (s >= 0) q('uptime').textContent = Math.floor(s / 86400) + 'd ' + p(Math.floor(s / 3600) % 24) + ':' + p(Math.floor(s / 60) % 60) + ':' + p(s % 60);
+  });
+}
+
+/* ---------- log view ---------- */
+/* appGet answers {\n"nvram_dump-<file>":<raw text>\n}\n - not JSON; cut between the first '":' and the last "\n}" */
+function cut(t){ var a = t.indexOf('":'), b = t.lastIndexOf('\n}'); if (a < 0) return ''; return t.slice(a + 2, b > a ? b : t.length); }
+function render(){
+  var raw = lastText[view], box = q('logview');
+  if (raw === null){ box.textContent = ''; q('logmeta').textContent = ''; return; }
+  var lines = raw.split('\n'), want = q('find').value.trim().toLowerCase(), out = [], hidden = 0, i, l;
+  for (i = 0; i < lines.length; i++){
+    l = lines[i]; if (!l) continue;
+    if (view === 'sys' && FILTER.some(function(f){ return l.indexOf(f) >= 0; })){ hidden++; continue; }
+    if (want && l.toLowerCase().indexOf(want) < 0) continue;
+    out.push(l);
+  }
+  /* never yank the view while the reader has scrolled up to read something */
+  var atEnd = box.scrollHeight - box.scrollTop - box.clientHeight < 24;
+  box.textContent = out.join('\n');
+  if (atEnd) box.scrollTop = box.scrollHeight;
+  q('logmeta').textContent = out.length + ' ' + `<#RLOG_10#>` + (want ? ' (' + `<#RLOG_11#>` + ')' : '');
+}
+function load(force){
+  if (busy) return; busy = true;
+  var v = view, x = new XMLHttpRequest();
+  x.open('GET', '/appGet.cgi?hook=' + encodeURIComponent(HOOK[v]) + '&_=' + Date.now(), true);
+  x.timeout = 15000;
+  x.onload = function(){ busy = false; if (x.status === 200){ var t = cut(x.responseText); if (force || t !== lastText[v]){ lastText[v] = t; if (v === view) render(); } } };
+  x.onerror = x.ontimeout = function(){ busy = false; };
+  x.send();
+}
+function schedule(){
+  if (timer){ clearInterval(timer); timer = null; }
+  if (q('c_auto').checked) timer = setInterval(function(){ if (!document.hidden) load(false); }, 10000);   /* review 2026-10-24 (Q-C2-5): 10 s */
+}
+function setView(v){
+  view = v;
+  Array.prototype.forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('#wins .win'), function(w){ w.classList.toggle('on', w.getAttribute('data-v') === v); });
+  /* the login log has no Clear (stock had none: it is the record of who signed in) */
+  q('b_clear').style.display = v === 'sys' ? '' : 'none';
+  q('b_save').style.display = v === 'sys' ? '' : 'none';
+  render(); load(true);
+}
+
+/* ---------- settings ---------- */
+/* syslog priorities by number; log_level 8 = "all" (BusyBox syslogd -l 8) */
+function fillLevels(sel, from, to){ var h = '', i; for (i = from; i <= to; i++) h += '<option value="' + i + '">' + hx(LEVELS[i]) + '</option>'; sel.innerHTML = h; }
+function collect(){ return {log_ipaddr: q('i_log_ipaddr').value.trim(), log_port: q('i_log_port').value.trim(), message_loglevel: q('s_message_loglevel').value, log_level: q('s_log_level').value}; }
+function diff(c){ var ch = {}, k; for (k in c) if (String(c[k]) !== String(NV[k])) ch[k] = c[k]; return ch; }
+function dirty(){ var n = 0, k, ch = diff(collect()); for (k in ch) n++; q('discardbtn').disabled = !n; }
+function bad(id, m){ var el = q(id), row = el.closest('.frow'); row.classList.add('bad'); setTimeout(function(){ row.classList.remove('bad'); }, 6000); el.focus(); msg('setmsg', m); }
+function applySet(){
+  msg('setmsg', '');
+  var c = collect(), ch = diff(c), n = 0, k;
+  if (c.log_ipaddr && !(rp.v.ipv4(c.log_ipaddr) || rp.v.hostname(c.log_ipaddr))) return bad('i_log_ipaddr', `<#RADM_69#>`);
+  if (c.log_port && !rp.v.port(c.log_port)) return bad('i_log_port', `<#RADM_64#>`);
+  for (k in ch) n++;
+  if (!n){ msg('setmsg', `<#RADM_63#>`); return; }
+  rp.applying(`<#Reaper_c_applying#>`, `<#RADM_61#>`);
+  rp.post(document.form, ch, 'restart_logger', 5, false);
+  setTimeout(function(){ location.reload(); }, 9000);
+}
+
+/* ---------- wiring ---------- */
+function boot(){
+  try { clock(); } catch (e) {}
+  try {
+    q('i_log_ipaddr').value = NV.log_ipaddr; q('i_log_port').value = NV.log_port;
+    fillLevels(q('s_message_loglevel'), 0, 7); fillLevels(q('s_log_level'), 1, 8);
+    q('s_message_loglevel').value = NV.message_loglevel; q('s_log_level').value = NV.log_level;
+  } catch (e) { q('p_set').classList.add('broken'); q('applybtn').disabled = true; }
+  /* the stock page's client-side filter list lives in /ajax/logFilter.json; the copy above is the fallback */
+  try { var fx = new XMLHttpRequest(); fx.open('GET', '/ajax/logFilter.json', true);
+    fx.onload = function(){ try { var f = JSON.parse(fx.responseText).filter; if (f && f.length){ FILTER = f.map(String); render(); } } catch (e) {} }; fx.send(); } catch (e) {}
+  Array.prototype.forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('#wins .win'), function(w){ w.addEventListener('click', function(){ setView(w.getAttribute('data-v')); }); });
+  on('find', 'input', render);
+  on('c_auto', 'change', schedule);
+  on('b_refresh', 'click', function(){ load(true); });
+  on('b_save', 'click', function(){ location.href = '/syslog.txt'; });
+  on('b_clear', 'click', function(){
+    if (!confirm(`<#RLOG_12#>`)) return;
+    document.forms.clearform.submit(); lastText.sys = ''; render();
+    setTimeout(function(){ load(true); }, 1500);
+  });
+  on('applybtn', 'click', applySet);
+  on('discardbtn', 'click', function(){ location.reload(); });
+  ['i_log_ipaddr', 'i_log_port', 's_message_loglevel', 's_log_level'].forEach(function(id){ on(id, 'input', dirty); on(id, 'change', dirty); });
+  document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', function(){ if (!document.hidden && q('c_auto').checked) load(false); });
+  if (/[?&]view=login\b/.test(location.search)) setView('login'); else load(true);
+  schedule(); dirty();
+}
+boot();
+})();
+</script>
+</body>
+</html>
diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Reaper_NAT.asp b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_NAT.asp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..850cd7c143
--- /dev/null
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_NAT.asp
@@ -0,0 +1,648 @@
+<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+     Copyright (C) 2026 the Reaper project maintainer
+     Part of the Reaper hardened Asuswrt-Merlin build. See LICENSE / LICENSE.reaper. -->
+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+<meta charset="utf-8">
+<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
+<meta name="reaper-native" content="1">
+<title>REAPER &mdash; <#RNAT_01#></title>
+<!-- Reaper_NAT.asp - WAN > NAT and Port Forwarding (Reaper-native UI, LAN/WAN wave, 2026-10-23).
+     Replaces four stock pages, one tab each (parity files build-scripts/tests/ui_parity/<stock page>.json):
+       Port Forwarding  = Advanced_VirtualServer_Content.asp (vts_enable_x, vts_rulelist)
+       Port Trigger     = Advanced_PortTrigger_Content.asp (autofw_enable_x, autofw_rulelist)
+       DMZ              = Advanced_Exposed_Content.asp (dmz_ip)
+       NAT Passthrough  = Advanced_NATPassThrough_Content.asp (fw_pt_*, pppoerelay_unit, vts_ftpport)
+     The record formats are stock's: vts_rulelist <name>ext>ip>lport>proto>src (rc/firewall.c write_port_forwarding),
+     autofw_rulelist <desc>trigger port>proto>incoming port>proto (rc/firewall.c write_porttrigger). Rows nobody
+     edited are written back byte for byte. Every stock check is kept: port syntax and ranges, the 1-255 protocol
+     number for OTHER, IPv4 / IPv4-or-subnet, the duplicate rules, 64 / 32 row caps, the JP v6plus/OCN port-set
+     confirm, the FTP ALG port range.
+     Deliberate differences from stock:
+     - Nothing is saved before Apply. Stock saved every port-forward add/edit/delete and the enable switch at once
+       (applyapp.cgi), and the switch ran restart_firewall twice (applyapp + a form submit). Here one Apply posts
+       only the changed settings with one restart.
+     - Editing a forward runs the duplicate check too (stock checked new rules only), and the trigger editor
+       checks its incoming port the same way for new and edited rules.
+     - The external port is stored normalised (spaces and leading zeros removed, - and ~ written as :):
+       rc/firewall.c _fw_ports_ok() drops a rule whose port has a dash, which stock saved as typed. A range must
+       ascend (stock never checked it; rc drops a descending one).
+     - A list over its nvram size (vts_rulelist 8192, autofw_rulelist 2048 bytes, shared/defaults.c) is refused
+       here; httpd's nvram_check dropped it silently.
+     - Internal and DMZ addresses: the router's own address and the LAN network / broadcast addresses are refused;
+       an address off the LAN subnet asks first (stock checked neither).
+     - The ?af=KnownApps&item=ftp deep link opens the FTP preset in the editor; stock added and saved the rule on load.
+     - No stray wl_ssid field (stock NAT Passthrough posted it on every save); vts_ftpport is validated on every
