+<!-- Reaper_VPNClient.asp - VPN > VPN Client (Reaper-native UI, VPN wave, 2026-10-23).
+     Replaces Advanced_OpenVPNClient_Content.asp (tab ovpn, OpenVPN clients 1-5), Advanced_WireguardClient_Content.asp
+     (tab wg, WireGuard clients 1-5) and Advanced_VPNClient_Content.asp (tab pptp, the PPTP / L2TP client and its saved
+     servers). Parity files build-scripts/tests/ui_parity/{Advanced_OpenVPNClient_Content,Advanced_WireguardClient_Content,
+     Advanced_VPNClient_Content}.json. Only the changed settings are posted; nothing is written on load.
+     How the clients start on this build (RTCONFIG_VPN_FUSION + VPN_FUSION_MERLIN, inventory_B.md "CLIENT START-PATH MAP"):
+     - OpenVPN client N runs from vpn_clientN_* alone (libovpn/openvpn_config.c ovpn_get_cconf); enabled = N listed in
+       vpn_clientx_eas; start/stop/restart_vpnclientN (rc/services.c vpnclient); start_vpnroutingN re-applies VPN Director
+       routing, the killswitch (vpn_clientN_enforce) and exclusive DNS, then Policy Routing (reaper_pbr_regen).
+     - WireGuard client N runs from wgcN_* alone (rc/wireguard.c start_wgc); enabled = wgcN_enable; restart_wgc N / stop_wgc N;
+       routing is VPN Director only; start_vpnrouting0 re-applies every WG killswitch (wgcN_enforce).
+     - The PPTP / L2TP client is the legacy single client (rc/vpnc_legacy.c legacy_start_vpnc, via start_vpnc()): it runs from
+       vpnc_proto, vpnc_heartbeat_x, vpnc_pppoe_username / passwd, vpnc_pptp_options_x, vpnc_dnsenable_x, vpnc_defroute_x and
+       auto-starts on WAN up when vpnc_auto_conn=1 (rc/wan.c:4538). vpnc_clientlist + vpnc_pptp_options_x_list are the saved
+       servers only (rc/format.c normalises them at boot). vpnc_dev_policy_list has no effective reader: not carried.
+     Deliberate differences from stock:
+     - OpenVPN: the instance selector keeps the stock apply.cgi change_vpn_client_unit round trip (vpn_client_unit also selects
+       the /jffs custom-config file httpd serves); keys and certificates come from ajax_openvpn_server.asp parsed line by line
+       (stock evaluated it as script, B-OVPNC-3); the dead Local/remote endpoint and Tunnel address rows are gone (B-OVPNC-2);
+       the server address is required when the client is enabled (B-OVPNC-4); ";;restart_dnsmasq" is one separator (B-OVPNC-1).
+     - WireGuard: Apply restarts only the edited client (restart_wgc N; stock restart_wgc restarted all five, B-WGC-1) and stops
+       a client that was turned off (start_wgc ignores wgcN_enable); the instance switch is client-side; address / DNS fields
+       take the nvram sizes (B-WGC-2); DNS servers must be addresses (rc routes them, B-WGC-3); a disabled client is still
+       validated (B-WGC-4); Allowed IPs has a visible, enforced byte cap (wgcN_aips is not on the JFFS whitelist, B-WGC-5).
+     - PPTP / L2TP: one connection panel on the keys the client actually reads (plus the Use server's DNS and Route all
+       traffic switches rc already honoured) and a saved-servers list; new saves write MPPE 128-bit only (no "No encryption",
+       no MPPE-40 / Auto, B-VPNC-2), a saved weaker value stays until re-saved and is marked; passwords are masked (B-VPNC-3);
+       turning the client off keeps its settings (B-VPNC-4); the options list always has one entry per row (B-VPNC-5);
+       untouched rows are written back byte for byte, new rows in the shape rc/format.c produces (B-VPNC-6).
+       restart_vpncall is the only dispatch that reaches legacy_start_vpnc; on this build it also stops every OpenVPN client
+       (services.c vpncall, B-VPNC-1) - the rc fix is listed in REPORT.md and must ship with this page. -->
