+<!-- Reaper_VPNServer.asp - VPN Server (Reaper-native UI, VPN wave, 2026-10-23).
+     Replaces Advanced_VPN_OpenVPN.asp, Advanced_WireguardServer_Content.asp, Advanced_VPN_IPSec.asp,
+     Advanced_VPN_PPTP.asp and the VPNS_V2 app scripts (sysdep/FUNCTION/VPNS_V2/VPN/vpns_*.js) hosted by
+     Advanced_VPNServer_Content.asp (parity files build-scripts/tests/ui_parity/Advanced_VPN_OpenVPN.json,
+     Advanced_WireguardServer_Content.json, Advanced_VPN_IPSec.json, Advanced_VPN_PPTP.json,
+     Advanced_VPNServer_Content.json). Four tabs: OpenVPN (2 instances), WireGuard, IPsec, PPTP; a tab hides where
+     menu.js hid the stock page (openvpnd / wireguard / ipsec_srv / pptpd). Deep link: ?tab=ovpn|wg|ipsec|pptp.
+     Only the changed settings are posted; nothing is written on load. The one non-Apply write is the stock
+     instance cursor (vpn_server_unit via apply.cgi change_vpn_server_unit; wgsc_unit via chg_wgsc_unit) that
+     httpd's cert editor / client-key / peer-export endpoints key on - written only on the user's click, as stock.
+     Deliberate differences from stock:
+     - OpenVPN: every list is serialised from a model (stock re-read table innerHTML, B-OVPN-2); the per-client
+       list (vpn_serverN_ccd_val) is byte-capped because the key is not on the JFFS whitelist (B-OVPN-1); CN,
+       subnet/mask, local/remote endpoints and the cipher list are validated (B-OVPN-3..6); two instances cannot
+       share a port+protocol (B-OVPN-7); subnet conflicts use real overlap tests (B-OVPN-8); the custom config and
+       the key files are posted unindexed with vpn_server_unit so they land in /jffs/openvpn files, never nvram;
+       the ajax endpoints are parsed, never eval'd (B-OVPN-10).
+     - WireGuard: deleting a peer blanks its keys AND restarts the server (stock's live removal failed because the
+       public key was blanked first, B-WGS-2, and a disabled slot kept its key pair, B-WGS-4); the server restart is
+       always the unit-less restart_wgs (restart_wgs 1 ignores wgs1_enable, B-WGS-5); the server is never enabled
+       behind the user's back (stock auto-enabled it on the first peer, B-WGS-6); enabling seeds the stock defaults
+       into indexed keys that were never written (rc reads wgs1_*, defaults exist only as wgs_*).
+     - IPsec: the profile strings are regenerated only after an edit (stock re-posted them on every Apply,
+       B-IPSEC-1); passwords never sit in title attributes (B-IPSEC-2); the virtual subnet is checked against the
+       LAN, OpenVPN, PPTP and WireGuard ranges (B-IPSEC-4); a saved Instant Guard profile is shown read-only with a
+       one-click removal (its page is gone).
+     - PPTP: authentication is fixed to MS-CHAPv2 with MPPE-128 required (pptpd_chap=2, pptpd_mppe=1; MS-CHAPv1,
+       MPPE-40 and "No encryption" are no longer offered, B-PPTP-5); one manual DNS / WINS server is enough
+       (B-PPTP-2); a client range that contains the router's LAN address is refused (B-PPTP-3). -->
